{"tool_name":"clustperturb","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"clustperturb","home":"https://rstacey.shinyapps.io/clust-perturb-tool/","license":"MIT","summary":"On the robustness of graph-based clustering to random network alterations.\n\nclust.perturb is an R package designed to test the robustness of graph-based clusters by randomly rewiring a portion of the underlying network and reclustering. Robust clusters \u201cstick together\u201d even after network rewiring, while non-robust clusters do not. Robustness is quantified using maximum Jaccard index.","addition_date":"2021-01-18T08:42:03Z","last_update_date":"2021-02-12T16:08:52Z","biotools_curie":"biotools:clustperturb","credit":[{"email":"richard.greg.stacey@gmail.com","name":"R. Greg Stacey","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Clustering","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3432"},{"term":"Network visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3925"},{"term":"Pathway analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3928"}]}],"name":"clust.perturb","owner":"zsmag19","publication":[{"doi":"10.1101/2020.04.24.059758"}],"topic":[{"term":"Molecular interactions, pathways and networks","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0602"},{"term":"Proteomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0121"},{"term":"Sequencing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3168"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"clust.perturb","home":"https://bio.tools/clustperturb","license":"MIT","summary":"On the robustness of graph-based clustering to random network alterations.\n\nclust.perturb is an R package designed to test the robustness of graph-based clusters by randomly rewiring a portion of the underlying network and reclustering. Robust clusters \u201cstick together\u201d even after network rewiring, while non-robust clusters do not. Robustness is quantified using maximum Jaccard index.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb"